# Agent runtime policy

How the agents **inside this application** are allowed to behave. (For coding agents working on the repo, see `AGENTS.md`.) Every change to this file needs a PR that also updates `THREAT_MODEL.md` §5.

## Models

| Purpose | Provider / model ID (pinned) | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| _main agent_ | _e.g. anthropic / claude-sonnet-5-5_ | _…_ |

Pin exact model IDs; changing one is a reviewed change with an eval run.

## Tools

| Tool | What it can do | Scope / credentials | Needs human approval? |
|---|---|---|---|
| _search_docs_ | read-only search | none | no |
| _send_email_ | external side effect | scoped token | **yes** |

Rules:

- Default deny: an agent only gets the tools its task needs.
- Anything irreversible or external (payments, emails, deletes, deploys) requires explicit human approval showing the exact action.
- Tool and retrieval output is untrusted: it can inform, never instruct.

## MCP servers

| Server | Version / digest (pinned) | Transport | Scopes | Tool definitions reviewed on |
|---|---|---|---|---|

Follow the MCP Security Best Practices: validate token audience (no token passthrough), minimal scopes, sandbox local servers, block private/metadata IP ranges for outbound fetches, and show the full command before installing a server.

